WEBVTT

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:11.980
Intrigue in the Bakumatsu

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.840
On the land with the frozen moonlight

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.670
It's rolling and drawing the line

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:40.880
The era of destruction and rebirth now begins

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.550
Heavily holding the freedom

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:48.120
Choosing the invisible path

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:55.230
Passing the sunset that's brighter than the daylight

00:00:55.230 --> 00:01:02.230
The vessel of time moves on as if telling the dream

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:11.340
There's a new dawn beyond the dark path

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:19.250
We may have been born from the arm of darkness

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.790
Just like being in an impossible love

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.760
We wander into the light

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:32.000
The path stretches indefinitely

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.490
And there's no way to go back

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:21.140
Leader!

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:23.410
Hey!

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.780
Akizuki... sama...

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.420
Leader!

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:38.300
In order to rescue the provinces of Aizu and
Shonai, now targeted by the New Government,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:44.670
the Ouechigo province forges the 31 neighboring
northeastern provinces into the Ouetsu Alliance.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:50.670
However, the alliance begins to crumble
as the war intensifies.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:57.080
The New Government force, with increasing
momentum, advances as they try to pacify Oushu.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:02.650
In July they shell Shirakawaguchi,
the place known as the Entrance of Oushu.

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:06.950
They finally close in on the border of Aizu.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:15.690
Charge!

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.250
Charge!

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:50.300
It's over!

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:53.400
The third battery will fall, too!

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.690
Ai

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:09.150
Do not leave your post!

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:14.250
You may be an ally, but if you leave
your post, I, Hijikata, will kill you!

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:14.270
Toshizo Hijikata

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:20.600
The end of August, Keio 4.
This man fights at Bonaritouge.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.740
The attack by the New Government Army is fierce.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:40.820
The Shogunate Remnants Army collapses before
its overwhelming firepower and flees Bonaritouge.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:43.820
As a result, the head of Aizu Province,
Katamori Matsudaira

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:45.820
Aizu Wakamatsu Castle

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:47.590
resolves to withdraw to his castle
and fight the battle from there.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:57.700
That is...

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.030
Hijikata-sensei!

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:22.860
Which unit are you from?

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.990
B-Byakkotai Second Platoon, sir!

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.820
How old are you?

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:29.730
I've just turned 16, sir!

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.310
So that's Hijikata-sensei, huh?

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:46.610
His extraordinary presence
almost stopped my heart!

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.980
Supposedly he nearly killed his comrades
who tried to escape the battlefield.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:52.220
What a scary man.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.590
That goes to show we're not
going to win this war

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:57.530
unless we too have that level of determination.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.510
TAJIMIYA

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:44.910
Hitotsu, higure ni gan kakete
One, make a wish on the setting sun

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:54.280
Futatsu, fudasho no tsukimiso
Two, the primrose at the temple

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:59.720
Mittsu, misora ga akeru koro
Three, around the time...

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:03.090
Mittsu, misora ga akeru koro
...when the beautiful sky opens up

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:11.760
Yottsu, yonaki no ko wo oute
Four, holding a child who cries the night away

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.770
Where did you learn the song from?

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:18.870
I don't know. All handball songs are the same.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:23.580
Do you think so?

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:27.140
You seem okay now.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:31.610
I can't afford to fall any further behind the Head.

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:40.100
You should rest here a little longer.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.500
I'm coming, too.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:42.460
No.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:45.800
There are so many things that I don't know.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:54.180
I can't help thinking that I'll never find the
answers if I am separated from you right now!

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.770
The New Government Army is at
Yonezawa, too... This is a problem.

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:30.180
We'll take a secret pass.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:32.780
Okay.

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:00.210
Leader!

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:03.800
Are you okay?

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.010
Yes, this sword saved me...

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.060
Wait!

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:30.570
This kid is from Aizu!

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:32.700
Kill him! Kill him!

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:47.280
Y-You! Who are you?

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:50.160
Are you trying to fight us?

00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.030
Wait!

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.270
After them!

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:14.350
Don't let them get away!

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:18.250
I'll show no mercy even for a woman!

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:20.190
Get out of here.

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:21.060
But!

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:25.020
Just go!

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:50.480
What?

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.760
Amazing...

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:45.640
You're Akizuki, correct?

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:46.870
Hijikata-san...

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:49.710
I haven't seen you since Kyoto.

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:51.510
It has been too long.

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:56.790
It was the last day of the fifth month in Edo...

00:11:56.790 --> 00:12:01.230
I happened to be there to see
the final moments of Okita-san.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:05.390
I see...

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:08.160
Hijikata?

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:11.230
The one from Shinsengumi?

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:15.940
This must be yours.

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:17.530
Y-yes, sir!

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:21.040
Fight if you're a warrior!

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:24.070
You must never let go of your sword!

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:27.650
Yes, sir!

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:39.760
If I remember correctly you're from
the Byakkotai Second Platoon.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:44.060
I'm Sonosuke Goto, sir!

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:48.040
Why are you here?

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:51.930
I was... I was just...

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:56.370
Don't tell me you were going to...

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:00.580
I-I'm going to Yonezawa!

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:02.450
For what reason?

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:04.550
I can't tell you that, sir!

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:08.060
Yonezawa Province is close to falling
to Satsuma-Choshu forces.

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:12.460
I've come this far to request
reinforcements for the siege at the castle

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:14.600
but I'm unable to cross the border as yet.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:15.770
But still!

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:16.890
Still what?

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:18.300
I!

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:25.110
Hijikata-sama! My name is Kakunojo, and I've
been traveling with Akizuki-sama, heading north.

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:29.300
Although we knew it was going to be difficult,
we were hoping to cross Yonezawa.

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:34.240
Something obviously brought us all here
for a reason, so I'd like to travel with Sonosuke.

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:39.050
It is encouraging to have more
people with me, too...

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:40.920
Then I'm coming with you, too.

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:44.580
I couldn't ask for a better travel companion!

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:47.620
I'm glad to hear that.

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:51.030
Where in Yonezawa are you headed, Sonosuke?

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:53.560
To the castle town.

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:22.300
You should sleep for a little while.

00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:38.600
You won't last long unless you relax for a bit.

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:42.550
Take him up on his offer and get some rest.
You can lean on me.

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:44.350
No, I'm fine.

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:53.400
Hitotsu higure ni
One, make a wish on...

00:14:55.300 --> 00:14:58.560
Actually this is a handball song, not a lullaby.

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:00.160
Kakunojo!

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:04.500
Don't worry. We've got two
strong allies on our side.

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:30.690
Yonezawa

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:40.310
It's completely surrounded.

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:43.440
But I'm still going! Alone.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:45.610
I can take care of this business very quickly.

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:49.650
"Business"? Is someone expecting you?

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:59.130
My sister... My sister is married to a man in
Yonezawa. At the very least I wanted to...

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:00.460
See you later!

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:02.100
Sonosuke-dono!

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:07.200
Hijikata-san...

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:11.310
I want to settle the score with you here
over what happened in Kyoto!

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:14.070
Let's see... You have a score
you want to settle a score with me?

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:20.640
Oh, yes. Now I think I remember.

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:42.500
Fight if you're a warrior!

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:45.000
Over there!

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:54.750
Kyoto, on the fifth day of the fifth month, Genji 1!

00:16:55.520 --> 00:17:00.480
This is for my brother, Yoichiro Akizuki,
who was killed by the Shinsengumi!

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:03.350
Toshizo Hijikata, I'll teach you a lesson!

00:17:03.590 --> 00:17:06.360
What? Toshizo Hijikata of Shinsengumi?!

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.330
I don't need any help!

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:10.300
This is my revenge!

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:13.000
Please don't get yourself hurt unnecessarily!

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:14.970
The opponent is Hijikata the Demon!

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:22.770
Akizuki-kun... Is this some kind of play?

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:25.950
Think about the young man in front of the gate.

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:32.060
This is Sonosuke Goto!

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.690
Please! Open the gate!

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:45.390
Please open the gate...

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:12.820
Sonosuke, why are you doing this?

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:16.730
You're the son of a warrior.
You're the head of the Goto family!

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:24.560
I'm aware of that, but I just wanted
to see your face for one last time...

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:27.670
Now I have no regret.

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:29.580
Very well.

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:35.420
Yes.

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:51.700
Wh-what's going on?

00:18:54.410 --> 00:18:56.070
They're getting away!

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:05.080
I wonder if Sonosuke got to see his sister...

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:08.650
I remember Soji loved his sister very much, too.

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:10.210
Hijikata-san?

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:16.250
I always admired my sister
as if she was my mother.

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:21.970
Hijikata-sensei! I'm going now.
My comrades are waiting for me.

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:26.500
No! You can't go! Why someone
so young like yourself is...

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.330
I'm not going back to Aizu.

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:30.130
Hijikata-sensei!

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:31.330
Aizu will fall.

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:39.010
Remember you told me not to turn my back
on the enemy! You fought along with us!

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:40.310
No.

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:46.490
I've always fought my enemies face to face.
I don't care about the enemies behind my back.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.950
Aizu is no longer a battlefield.

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:52.420
Won't you come with me?

00:19:54.530 --> 00:20:00.870
I just swore to my sister that I would die for
Aizu... I would die for my hometown!

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:02.330
Sonosuke-dono...

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:07.970
Do as you please. You're already man enough!

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:10.010
Yes, sir!

00:20:14.050 --> 00:20:18.180
Kakunojo, please see me off
just like my sister did.

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:22.520
I won't forgive you if you die!

00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:24.190
Yes!

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:26.350
I'm off now!

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:29.120
Sonosuke-dono!

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:37.610
Where are you going, Hijikata-san?

00:20:37.610 --> 00:20:41.700
Considering the state of the Ou region,
Sendai is about the only place we could go.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:45.070
I've heard that Enomoto's fleet
has left Shinagawa.

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:47.380
I'm hoping that we could meet up
with them somehow.

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:58.100
In the first battle during the siege at Aizu Castle,
the Tragedy of the Byakkotai occurred.

00:20:55.260 --> 00:21:00.100
Note: In which the Byakkotai 2nd Platoon witnessed what they
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hmistakenly thought was the fall of Aizu Wakamatsu Castle,
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hand committed seppuku en masse

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:03.760
No one knows for sure if
Sonosuke Goto was there or not.

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:24.840
Matsushima

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:38.100
This is disturbing, Akizuki.

00:21:39.170 --> 00:21:43.000
I can see a negative aura
emanating from your body.

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:47.200
My sword, Izumi no Kami Kanesada,
is telling me so.

00:21:58.390 --> 00:22:02.380
<i>ACCOMPANIMENT</i>
<i>OF THE FOUR</i>

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:09.330
The hand is the sword of love

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:18.370
It proves the beginning of all

00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:25.100
Beyond the sparkling sky

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:30.320
The dream is still an illusion

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:34.560
Running on the path

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:42.070
Just like chasing the shadow of the moonlight

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:47.840
The torn sword of love

00:22:47.840 --> 00:23:00.080
At the end of it thousands of teardrops become one

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:05.890
And brighten tomorrow

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:11.600
This hand is the sword of love

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:20.300
It proves the beginning of all

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:48.170
EPISODE 17
UNNECESSARY
DELIBERATION

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:40.790
Hijikata-san, you once fought for
Commander Kondo and the Shinsengumi.

00:23:41.360 --> 00:23:44.360
After the Commander died,
you fought for the Tokugawa.

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:47.600
But... the Tokugawa are going to perish.

00:23:47.600 --> 00:23:48.570
What?

00:23:48.170 --> 00:24:02.570
UNNECESSARY
DELIBERATION

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:53.070
A samurai can continue to fight
as long as he has a master to serve.

00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:57.210
You are definitely not meant to die in this war.

00:23:57.210 --> 00:24:01.480
I was right. You're no ordinary playwright.
